<title>USA: Planet Hollywood Q4 shr rises.</title>
<headline>Planet Hollywood Q4 shr rises.</headline>
<dateline>ORLANDO, Fla. 1997-02-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>1996			1995</p>
<p> Shr		 $0.13		    $nil</p>
<p> Net		 14,158		   251</p>
<p> Revs		99,133		   74,997</p>
<p> Avg shrs	  110,364		  86,814</p>
<p>	  12 MONTHS</p>
<p> Shr		 $0.37		    $0.24</p>
<p> Net		 37,659		   20,727</p>
<p> Revs		373,364		  270,606</p>
<p> Avg shrs	  103,055		  86,814</p>
<p>(All data above 000s except per share numbers)</p>
<p>Full company name is Planet Hollywood International Inc</p>
<p>NOTE: Net income for full-year 1996 results include a one time charge of $10.4 million, net of $5.9 million in taxes, due to the extinguishment of long-term payable notes.</p>
<p>The number of shares increased in 1996 from 1995 due to the completion of the company's initial public offering on April 24, 1996, it said.</p>
<p>((New York newsdesk 212-859-1610))</p>
